          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. As per Eq. (4.2a), by dividing the change in position (BC) by the change in time (CA), you get the average velocity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.126,
            0.488,
            0.164
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_1.jpg",
          "content": "\\nu = \\frac{s_{2} - s_{1}}{t_{2} - t_{1}} = \\frac{\\overline{BC}}{CA}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.168,
            0.888,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. By extracting values of time "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and distances "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "S _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "S _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from the graph, the magnitude of average velocity can be calculated as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.354,
            0.206,
            0.658,
            0.243
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "v=\\frac{80\\  m -40\\  m }{4\\  s -2\\  s }=\\frac{40\\  m }{2\\  s }=20\\  m \\  s ^{-1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.246,
            0.888,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From a position-time graph, by finding the positions of the object at two instants of time, you can calculate the average velocity by using Eq. (4.2a)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.282,
            0.889,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Geometrically, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { C A } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is called the slope of line AB connecting initial"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.317,
            0.89,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "position A and final position B in Fig. 4.14. The slope of a line is the steepness of the line. The slope of a graph gives information about the rate of change of the quantity shown on Y-axis with respect to the quantity shown on X-axis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.364,
            0.144,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.084,
                0.364,
                0.144,
                0.437
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.374,
            0.361,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ready to Go Beyond"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.396,
            0.815,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For the case of a curve also, the velocity at any instant can be calculated geometrically from the position-time graph. You will learn how to do it in higher grades."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
