          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4.6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " What does the graph shown in Fig. 4.15 indicate about the nature of motion of the vehicle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.489,
            0.89,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The position of the vehicle is 40 m from the origin and is not changing with time. Thus, the vehicle is at rest at 40 m from the origin. A straight line parallel to the time axis on a position-time graph represents a stationary object (In this case, the position-time graph is not the distance-time graph)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.689,
            0.472,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.052,
                0.576,
                0.218,
                0.606
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 4.15: Position-time graph of a vehicle"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.235,
                0.578,
                0.89,
                0.685
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Example 4.7:",
                  "styles": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": " The position-time graphs of two objects A and B are given in Fig. 4.16a. The magnitude of average velocity of which object is higher? "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Answer:",
                  "styles": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": " By making lines parallel to axes as shown in Fig. 4.16b, it is found that the displacement of object B is more than object A for the same time interval. That is, the slope of line for B is steeper than the slope for line A. Thus, the velocity of B is higher than that of A."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
